**12. CONFIDENTIALITY**

12.1 Each Party (the “Receiving Party”) shall keep confidential and shall not, without the prior written consent of the other Party (the “Disclosing Party”), disclose or make available to any person, or use for its own benefit or for the benefit of any other person, any Confidential Information of the Disclosing Party. For the purposes of this Agreement, “Confidential Information” means all information (whether written, oral, or in electronic form) disclosed by or on behalf of the Disclosing Party to the Receiving Party, or otherwise obtained by the Receiving Party, in connection with this Agreement, including but not limited to: (i) the terms of this Agreement; (ii) the Disclosing Party’s business plans, financial data, pricing structures, customer lists, supplier lists, recipes, specifications, and proprietary processes; (iii) any information marked as confidential; and (iv) any information which, from the circumstances of disclosure, a reasonable person would understand to be confidential.

12.2 The obligations in Clause 12.1 shall not apply to any information which:

(a) is or becomes generally available to the public other than as a result of a breach of this Clause 12;

(b) was available to the Receiving Party on a non-confidential basis before its disclosure by the Disclosing Party;

(c) becomes available to the Receiving Party on a non-confidential basis from a source other than the Disclosing Party, provided that such source is not bound by a confidentiality obligation to the Disclosing Party; or

(d) is required to be disclosed by law, by any court of competent jurisdiction, or by any regulatory or governmental authority, provided that, to the extent permitted by law, the Receiving Party gives the Disclosing Party prompt written notice of such required disclosure and cooperates with the Disclosing Party, at the Disclosing Party’s cost, in seeking a protective order or other appropriate remedy.

12.3 Each Party shall use Confidential Information of the other Party solely for the purpose of performing its obligations and exercising its rights under this Agreement.

12.4 The obligations of confidentiality under this Clause 12 shall survive the expiry or termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years, provided that, in respect of any Confidential Information that constitutes a trade secret, such obligations shall continue for so long as such information remains a trade secret.

**13. DATA PROTECTION**

13.1 The Parties acknowledge that, in the performance of this Agreement, the Supplier may process personal data on behalf of the Buyer in connection with the delivery of Products to the Buyer’s premises. The Parties shall comply with the Nigeria Data Protection Act, 2023, and any applicable regulations or guidance issued thereunder, in respect of any such processing.

13.2 The Supplier shall:

(a) process personal data only on the documented instructions of the Buyer, unless required to do otherwise by applicable law, in which case the Supplier shall inform the Buyer of that legal requirement before processing, unless that law prohibits such information on important grounds of public interest;

(b) ensure that persons authorised to process the personal data have committed themselves to confidentiality or are under an appropriate statutory obligation of confidentiality;

(c) implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk;

**14. WARRANTIES**

14.1 The Supplier warrants that, as at the date of this Agreement and throughout the Term:

(a) it has the full power and authority to enter into and perform this Agreement and to grant the rights granted under it;

(b) the Products shall conform in all material respects to the Product Specifications and any samples provided to the Buyer, and shall be of satisfactory quality, free from defects, and fit for the particular purpose for which they are required, being the preparation and service of food to the Buyer’s customers;

(c) the Products shall comply with all applicable laws, regulations, standards, and codes of practice, including the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control Act, Cap N1, Laws of the Federation of Nigeria, 2004, and any regulations made thereunder, and the Standards Organisation of Nigeria Act, Cap S9, Laws of the Federation of Nigeria, 2004;

(d) the Products shall be produced, stored, and transported in accordance with good manufacturing practices and the Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP) principles, and shall be delivered with a remaining shelf life of not less than seventy-five percent (75%) of the labelled shelf life, unless otherwise agreed in writing in respect of a particular delivery;

(e) the Supplier holds, and shall maintain throughout the Term, all licences, permits, and registrations necessary for the manufacture, storage, and supply of the Products, including any food safety management system certification required by law or by the Buyer’s reasonable request;

(f) the Products shall be free from any lien, charge, or encumbrance, and the Buyer shall obtain good and marketable title to the Products upon delivery and payment in accordance with this Agreement;

(g) the Supplier has not, and shall not during the Term, employed or engaged any person who is a child or who is subjected to forced labour, and the Supplier shall comply with all applicable labour laws and regulations in the Federal Republic of Nigeria in respect of its personnel engaged in the performance of this Agreement; and

(h) the Supplier shall not, in the performance of this Agreement, engage in any corrupt practice, bribery, or other unethical conduct, and shall comply with the provisions of the Corrupt Practices and Other Related Offences Act, Cap C31, Laws of the Federation of Nigeria, 2004.

14.2 The Supplier further warrants that the Products shall be supplied in accordance with the delivery schedule set out in Schedule 2, and that each delivery shall be accompanied by a delivery note stating the date of delivery, the product code, the quantity delivered, and the batch or lot number.

14.3 The Buyer shall notify the Supplier in writing of any breach of the warranties set out in this Clause 14 within seven (7) days of the date on which the Buyer becomes aware, or ought reasonably to have become aware, of such breach. Failure to give such notice shall not, however, operate as a waiver of the Buyer’s rights in respect of such breach.

14.4 The Supplier shall, at its own cost, replace or refund the price of any Products which do not comply with the warranties set out in this Clause 14, provided that the Buyer has given notice in accordance with Clause 14.3. The Buyer may, at its option, require the Supplier to collect the non-conforming Products at the Supplier’s cost within seventy-two (72) hours of the Buyer’s notice.
